# wasp/README.md at main · wasp-lang/wasp
created: 2020-01-30, last updated: 2026-04-16, [Read more](https://github.com/wasp-lang/wasp/blob/main/README.md)

🔒 Full-stack Auth, 🖇️ RPC (Client <-> Server), 🚀 Simple Deployment, ⚙ ️Jobs, ✉️ Email Sending, 🛟 Full-stack Type Safety, ...Simple Wasp config file in which you describe the high-level details of your web app:
```
// file: main.wasp
app todoApp {
title: "ToDo App", // visible in the browser tab
wasp: { version: "^0.15.0" },
auth: { // full-stack auth out-of-the-box
userEntity: User, methods: { email: {...} }
}
}
route RootRoute { path: "/", to: MainPage }
page MainPage {
authRequired: true, // Limit access to logged-in users.
...
}
...
entities: [Task] // Automatic cache invalidation.
}
// file: schema.prisma
model Task { // Your Prisma data model.
id Int @id @default(autoincrement())
description String
isDone Boolean @default(false)
}
```
The rest of the code you write in React / Node.js / Prisma and just reference it from the .wasp file.

